// root.cst — the stub root libcstd.csl is built through.
//
// The base runtime: the syscall bindings (std/os/causticos.cst) and the program
// helpers on top of them (std/causticos/prog.cst). Between them they are in
// almost every binary on the image — 77 and 66 of them — which made them the
// two biggest duplications in the tree after the font.
//
// A --shared build exports everything it defines, so importing the two modules
// is enough; the call below exists to give the linker an entry point to keep,
// not to enumerate a surface.
//
// Why this is a SEPARATE library from libfutil rather than one big one: a .csl
// cannot import from another .csl (the format has no import table for it), so
// libfutil necessarily contains the parts of these two it uses. Programs link
// against exactly one of the two, so nothing resolves ambiguously and no
// program maps more than it needs.
use "std/causticos/prog.cst" as p;
use "std/os/causticos.cst" as s;

fn _keep() as i64 { p.outs(cast(*u8, "")); return s.getpid(); }
